{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you","id":1363203,"title":"Totemic benefits of different animals with a breakdown of Totemic charms to help you","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-24T15:09:49-08:00","id":1363203,"title":"Totemic benefits of different animals with a breakdown of Totemic charms to help you","content":"There's a lot of Totemic charms. I thought, as we have the thread about powerful animal forms for fighting in, I'd like to look at what Totemic charms different animals give you.<br /> <br /> (I'll be honest: I have a kind of vague concept for a new Lunar character, but it works with any Totem. But any Lunar character whose Totem isn't important to the character is, frankly, a rubbish and unthematic character IMO. So I'm looking for inspiration. And this is also so I can myself work out what gets what. But I hope others will also find this thread useful.)<br /> <br /> Firstly of course, there's HBR and DBT, and the charm for permanently making a testing ground to create beastmen.<br /> <br /> Then there's the <u>Totemic benefits:</u><br /> <br /> First, the &quot;fluff&quot;-based ones.<br /> <br /> Animals that hunt in packs (doesn't need a &quot;Pack Hunter&quot; merit) = an absolute ton of war charms (from App and Cha) via Strength, and Diving Hawk Inspiration (App) via Dex. It also lets you get a bunch more (from Int) as Stamina charms.<br /> <br /> Hive-dwelling shapes = Wasp-and-Termite Dance (App) as a Charisma charm, and Living Hive Transformation (Dex) as a Stamina charm.<br /> <br /> Animal shapes that can look like other animals = Essential Mirror Nature&gt;One of the Herd&gt;Scent-of-all-Nations&gt;Cuckoo's Nest Hospitality&gt;Fickle Lady's Shifting Star&gt;Dreams-and-Expectations Stance&gt;Shifting Constellation Raiment (App) as Manipulation charms.<br /> Also, The Shadow Who Wasn't There&gt;Ever-Present Shadow Insinuation&gt;Countless Shadow-Puppets Dance (Man) as Appearance charms.<br /> <br /> Animals that can stick or adhere to sheer surfaces = Spider-Climbing Attitude as a Wits charm.<br /> <br /> Carrion Eaters = Plague-Swallowing Kiss as a Stamina charm.<br /> <br /> Migratory totem forms = Silver Curtain Parted (Per) as a Wits charm.<br /> Also Lodestone Reckoning Manner&gt;Dauntless Yeddim Caravan+Moon-Cloaked Wanderer&gt;Monarch-Wing Migration&gt;Albatross-and-Hurricane Odyssey+Treading Midnight's Road (Wits) as Perception charms.<br /> <br /> Water-breathing totems = Shifting Breath Inversion (Stam) as a Wits charm.<br /> <br /> Now onto the <u>Merit-based and dice pool-based ones</u>. I'll slowly have a look, but I'm hoping others will go &quot;oh yeah, such-and-such obscure an animal has 2 or 3 of these&quot;.<br /> <br /> Poisonus or toxic animals = Scorpion-and-Toad Absolution&gt;Adder-Fang Method&gt;Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery&gt;Poison Blood Prana (Stam) as Wits charms.<br /> Also get Blood-and-Tear Elixir Cultivation (Stam) as an Int charm.<br /> <br /> Camouflage = Moon's Hidden Face (App) and Ranging Wolf Deception (Wits) as Manipulation charms<br /> <br /> A Threaten or Intimidation dice pool on the totem animal = Lion's Voice Command&gt;Lion's Roar Rebuke (Cha) as Strength charms.<br /> Also gets Nightmare Scar Memento (Str) as a Charisma charm.<br /> <br /> Berzerker = Lessons of the Winter Wolf&gt;Wolf-Pack Training Technique&gt;Starving Beast Bloodthirst (Cha) as Stamina charms.<br /> <br /> Beast of Burden = Unyielding Brute Will (Str) as a Stamina charm.<br /> <br /> Vision-enhancing merits = Hunter's Eye Precision&gt;Bird's-Fall-From-Flock Targeting&gt;Deadly Raptor's Flight&gt;Heart-Piercing Instinct&gt;Great Huntress Mastery (Dex) as Perception charms.<br /> <br /> Tiny or Miniscule = Snake Finger Style+Night Stalker Approach&gt;Thieving Magpie Approach (Dex) as Manipulation charms and Clouds Cover Moon&gt;Candle-Eating Rat Trick (Man) as Dex charms.<br /> Also Cunning Anglerfish Decoy&gt;Ant-and-Starfish Trick (Dex) as a Manipulation or Wits charm.<br /> <br /> Tiny or Miniscule (prey only) totems = Captivating Siren Voice&gt;Argent Anglerfish Lure (Cha) as Appearance charms, and Observed Prey Instinct (Per) as a Dex charm.<br /> <br /> Miniscule size = Emerald Grasshopper Form&gt;Tyrant Mouse Dominion and Emerald Grasshopper Form&gt;Thousandfold Wasp Dance&gt;Hungry All-Consuming Cloud&gt;Locust-and-Starling Legion (Dex) as Wits charms.<br /> <br /> Legendary Size = Towering Beast Form&gt;Mountainous Spirit Expression&gt;Undaunted Behemoth Avatar (Str) as Stamina charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-29-2020, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T18:36:59-08:00","id":1363230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you#post1363203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now onto the <u>Merit-based and dice pool-based ones</u>. I'll slowly have a look, but I'm hoping others will go &quot;oh yeah, such-and-such obscure an animal has 2 or 3 of these&quot;.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tiny/Miniscule Octopuses hit a lot of them.<br /> <br /> -Water Breathing<br /> -Venomous<br /> -Camouflage<br /> -Vision-Enhancing<br /> -Tiny/Miniscule<br /> -Animal shapes that can look like other animals if you're a mimic octopus (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mimic_octopus\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mimic_octopus</a>)<br /> <br /> Could work well for a Manipulation-favoured No-Moon.<br /> <br /> Edit: Poison frogs hit all those except the last one (mimicry) as well.<br /> <br /> Lions get a few as well:<br /> <br /> -Hunt in Packs<br /> -Camouflage<br /> -Threated/Intimidation Pool<br /> -Vision-enhancing merit (Night Vision)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 01-25-2020, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T05:51:37-08:00","id":1363284,"title":"","content":"Octopus gives your HBR a lot of options too. Though I discovered, playing a snake-totem Lunar, that poison doesn't work great for HBR stuff; you can stack great mutations, but not the charms. Which, I mean, isn't bad (the poison-enhancing mutation is so, so good), but you're not going to be able to build your character around it.<br /> You can obviously just build it around having a brutal poison as a tiny little octopus of course...<br /> Also, I don't think that Extra Arms/Legs is that useful.<br /> <br /> Lions is a good point. I thought &quot;wait, isn't that the same for tigers, cheetahs, etc, they have the same stats&quot; but then tigers don't hunt in packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-25-2020, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:08:37-08:00","id":1363285,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... what are the best investments for HBR/DBT? Obviously that's dependent on your Totem.<br /> <br /> I guess Thick Hide, etc, is always good. Centaur is strong but very expensive. Wings is of course useful (especially for chimeras, stick it on top of your normal combat form), but again expensive.<br /> What do you guys think?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:44:40-08:00","id":1363290,"title":"","content":"Extra arms, ink sacs/smokescreen, and various toxin mutations all seem strong to me.<br /> <br /> Natural shield seems good specifically with crane style, especially combined with extra arms.<br /> <br /> Pheromones, Musical Voice, Imposing Features and Inhuman Visage are the social mutations<br /> <br /> I can imagine constrictor+entangling limbs as a grappling build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T06:57:25-08:00","id":1363293,"title":"","content":"I don't see Flurry used enough to make Extra Arms seem good?<br /> <br /> Or, more specifically, when I see flurries, they tend to be rush/something or disengage/something, which I guess you need Extra Legs for. Obviously an octopus-totem could take Extra Legs though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-25-2020, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T09:41:51-08:00","id":1363307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363285#post1363285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... what are the best investments for HBR/DBT? Obviously that's dependent on your Totem.<br /> <br /> I guess Thick Hide, etc, is always good. Centaur is strong but very expensive. Wings is of course useful (especially for chimeras, stick it on top of your normal combat form), but again expensive.<br /> What do you guys think?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, one of my fav topics.<br /> <br /> - As mentioned, the Natural Shield mutation lets you flurry full defences for cheap or free.<br /> <br /> - At 4 dots the improved natural weapon is expensive, especially given you aren\u2019t going to attack with it, but it does give you +1 to parry. (Stacks with Centaur too. You could just be tigerman-centaur and your natural parry could be +9)<br /> <br /> - I learned from the devs that Last Warriors Unity-Ing a pair of Razor Claws renders the hands unusable for other things in animal mode (via a strict reading of the rules) so you are gonna need another limb for that. I favour the tail and ambidextrous one dot mutation for a fully functioning and Disney-esque limb.<br /> <br /> More if I see them. Always remember, friends don\u2019t let friends take Carapace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-25-2020, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T10:04:53-08:00","id":1363310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363307#post1363307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always remember, friends don\u2019t let friends take Carapace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see an argument for taking it if it cost, like 1 dot. If you don't wear armour, and have Unnatural Hide 5 on your HBR, then it's kind of letting you put Medium Armour on as part of your transformation. But since you could just, you know, have medium armour (or artefact light armour), it's certainly too marginal for the cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T10:05:37-08:00","id":1363313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363307#post1363307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- As mentioned, the Natural Shield mutation lets you flurry full defences for cheap or free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering what forms could give you Natural Shield... crab, maybe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T10:44:16-08:00","id":1363316,"title":"","content":"So I thought I'd look at the animals my PCs play first:<br /> <br /> Walrus: Silver Curtain Parted (Per) as a Wits charm. Lodestone Reckoning Manner&gt;Dauntless Yeddim Caravan+Moon-Cloaked Wanderer&gt;Monarch-Wing Migration&gt;Albatross-and-Hurricane Odyssey+Treading Midnight's Road (Wits) as Perception charms. Lion's Voice Command&gt;Lion's Roar Rebuke (Cha) as Strength charms. Gets Nightmare Scar Memento (Str) as a Charisma charm.<br /> <br /> Gorilla: Lion's Voice Command&gt;Lion's Roar Rebuke (Cha) as Strength charms. Gets Nightmare Scar Memento (Str) as a Charisma charm.<br /> <br /> Toad: Shifting Breath Inversion (Stam) as a Wits charm. Scorpion-and-Toad Absolution&gt;Adder-Fang Method&gt;Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery&gt;Poison Blood Prana (Stam) as Wits charms.<br /> Also get Blood-and-Tear Elixir Cultivation (Stam) as an Int charm. Snake Finger Style+Night Stalker Approach&gt;Thieving Magpie Approach (Dex) as Manipulation charms and Clouds Cover Moon&gt;Candle-Eating Rat Trick (Man) as Dex charms.<br /> Also Cunning Anglerfish Decoy&gt;Ant-and-Starfish Trick (Wits) as a Manipulation or Wits charm. Captivating Siren Voice&gt;Argent Anglerfish Lure (Cha) as Appearance charms, and Observed Prey Instinct (Per) as a Dex charm.<br /> <br /> Polecat: Snake Finger Style+Night Stalker Approach&gt;Thieving Magpie Approach (Dex) as Manipulation charms and Clouds Cover Moon&gt;Candle-Eating Rat Trick (Man) as Dex charms.<br /> <br /> Aurochs: Unyielding Brute Will (Str) as a Stamina charm. Lion's Voice Command&gt;Lion's Roar Rebuke (Cha) as Strength charms.<br /> Also gets Nightmare Scar Memento (Str) as a Charisma charm.<br /> <br /> Poisonous spider: Scorpion-and-Toad Absolution&gt;Adder-Fang Method&gt;Mamba-and-Cobra Mastery&gt;Poison Blood Prana (Stam) as Wits charms.<br /> Also get Blood-and-Tear Elixir Cultivation (Stam) as an Int charm.<br /> Snake Finger Style+Night Stalker Approach&gt;Thieving Magpie Approach (Dex) as Manipulation charms and Clouds Cover Moon&gt;Candle-Eating Rat Trick (Man) as Dex charms.<br /> Also Cunning Anglerfish Decoy&gt;Ant-and-Starfish Trick (Dex) as a Manipulation or Wits charm. Spider-Climbing Attitude as a Wits charm.<br /> Emerald Grasshopper Form&gt;Tyrant Mouse Dominion and Emerald Grasshopper Form&gt;Thousandfold Wasp Dance&gt;Hungry All-Consuming Cloud&gt;Locust-and-Starling Legion (Dex) as Wits charms.<br /> <br /> Rabbit: Snake Finger Style+Night Stalker Approach&gt;Thieving Magpie Approach (Dex) as Manipulation charms and Clouds Cover Moon&gt;Candle-Eating Rat Trick (Man) as Dex charms.<br /> Also Cunning Anglerfish Decoy&gt;Ant-and-Starfish Trick (Dex) as a Manipulation or Wits charm. Captivating Siren Voice&gt;Argent Anglerfish Lure (Cha) as Appearance charms, and Observed Prey Instinct (Per) as a Dex charm.<br /> <br /> Poison and being really small seems to do a lot. Although I suspect a lot of characters with small totems favour Dex anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T11:14:46-08:00","id":1363322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363313#post1363313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering what forms could give you Natural Shield... crab, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crab, arguably turtle, Mollusc maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T01:00:10-08:00","id":1363420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363313#post1363313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering what forms could give you Natural Shield... crab, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crab, Scorpion, and maybe Lobster would be obvious choices.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363203-totemic-benefits-of-different-animals-with-a-breakdown-of-totemic-charms-to-help-you?p=1363322#post1363322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crab, arguably turtle, Mollusc maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is in the book. Vanamaithri Mirror-Soul has a giant tortoise spirit shape, and their Hybrid Body Transformation does grant Natural Shield. Remember the warform's mutation need not manifest in <i>quite</i> the same way they do on the spirit shape that inspires them.<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The mutation comes from having features like bony plates, enfolding wings, or such. So armadillos, pangolins, glypthodonts, could qualify in the same way.<br /> <br /> Swan would be excellent too.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T07:05:28-08:00","id":1365003,"title":"","content":"I feel as though Natural Shield including wings as something you can protect yourself with means that just about any animal shape with distinct limbs or bodily armour can provide the Merit, if one wishes to devote some of the points to it.<br /> <br /> Like, my Christmas Lunar's hybrid body manifests big ol' crow wings that are useless for flight but ward off attacks because the guy's persona puts keeping him alive first (and his hybrid form is meant to come across as a tad inelegant).<br /> <br /> In whatever form it takes, it is a supernaturally provided mutation after all, it doesn't strictly have to follow biological convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T13:31:58-07:00","id":1374792,"title":"","content":"Animals that mimic the appearance of another animal... anyone have any good ideas?<br /> <br /> Mimic octopus<br /> Hoverfly (they look like wasps)<br /> Those spiders that look like ants<br /> The butterfly that looks like an owl's face (or is it a moth?)<br /> <br /> What else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core